Here's how to handle multiple parent and child indexes with SIREN pagination using PIT:

## 1. Multiple Parent Indexes

When you have multiple parent indexes, you can open a PIT across all of them using index patterns or comma-separated values:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class MultiIndexSirenService {
    
    private final RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper = new ObjectMapper();
    private static final String ES_HOST = "http://localhost:9200";
    
    /**
     * Open PIT for multiple parent indexes
     */
    public String openPitForMultipleIndexes(List<String> parentIndexes, String keepAlive) {
        // Join multiple indexes with comma
        String indexPattern = String.join(",", parentIndexes);
        
        String url = String.format("%s/siren/%s/_pit?keep_alive=%s", 
            ES_HOST, indexPattern, keepAlive);
        
        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
        headers.setContentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON);
        HttpEntity<String> entity = new HttpEntity<>(headers);
        
        try {
            ResponseEntity<PitResponse> response = restTemplate.exchange(
                url, HttpMethod.POST, entity, PitResponse.class
            );
            
            String pitId = response.getBody().getId();
            log.info("Opened PIT for indexes {} with ID: {}", indexPattern, pitId);
            return pitId;
            
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Error opening PIT for multiple indexes", e);
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to open PIT", e);
        }
    }
}
```

### Usage Example:
```java
// Open PIT for multiple parent indexes
List<String> parentIndexes = Arrays.asList("machine-*", "server-*", "device-*");
String pitId = multiIndexService.openPitForMultipleIndexes(parentIndexes, "5m");
```

## 2. Multiple Child Indexes in Join

You can specify multiple child indexes in the join query:

```java
/**
 * Build join query with multiple child indexes
 */
private Map<String, Object> buildMultiChildJoinQuery(
        PaginationRequest paginationRequest,
        List<String> childIndexes,
        String parentField,
        String childField) {
    
    Map<String, Object> query = new HashMap<>();
    
    // Sort with tiebreaker
    Map<String, String> sort = new HashMap<>();
    sort.put("_shard_doc", "asc");
    query.put("sort", sort);
    
    // PIT
    if (paginationRequest.getPitId() != null) {
        Map<String, String> pit = new HashMap<>();
        pit.put("id", paginationRequest.getPitId());
        query.put("pit", pit);
    }
    
    // search_after
    if (paginationRequest.getSearchAfter() != null && 
        !paginationRequest.getSearchAfter().isEmpty()) {
        query.put("search_after", paginationRequest.getSearchAfter());
    }
    
    query.put("size", paginationRequest.getPageSize());
    
    // Build join with MULTIPLE child indexes
    Map<String, Object> joinQuery = new HashMap<>();
    joinQuery.put("indices", childIndexes);  // Multiple child indexes
    joinQuery.put("on", Arrays.asList(parentField, childField));
    
    // Child request with filter (optional)
    Map<String, Object> childRequest = new HashMap<>();
    Map<String, Object> matchAll = new HashMap<>();
    childRequest.put("query", Collections.singletonMap("match_all", matchAll));
    joinQuery.put("request", childRequest);
    
    Map<String, Object> outerQuery = new HashMap<>();
    outerQuery.put("join", joinQuery);
    query.put("query", outerQuery);
    
    return query;
}
```

## 3. Multiple Joins (Nested/Sequential)

For complex scenarios with multiple parent-child relationships:

```java
/**
 * Build query with multiple nested joins
 * Example: parent -> child1 -> child2
 */
private Map<String, Object> buildMultipleNestedJoins(
        PaginationRequest paginationRequest,
        MultiJoinConfig config) {
    
    Map<String, Object> query = new HashMap<>();
    
    // Sort and PIT
    Map<String, String> sort = new HashMap<>();
    sort.put("_shard_doc", "asc");
    query.put("sort", sort);
    
    if (paginationRequest.getPitId() != null) {
        query.put("pit", Collections.singletonMap("id", paginationRequest.getPitId()));
    }
    
    if (paginationRequest.getSearchAfter() != null) {
        query.put("search_after", paginationRequest.getSearchAfter());
    }
    
    query.put("size", paginationRequest.getPageSize());
    
    // Build nested join structure
    Map<String, Object> rootJoin = buildJoinLevel(
        config.getChild1Indexes(),
        config.getParentField(),
        config.getChild1Field(),
        // Nested join as part of child1 request
        buildJoinLevel(
            config.getChild2Indexes(),
            config.getChild1Field(),
            config.getChild2Field(),
            null  // No more nesting
        )
    );
    
    query.put("query", Collections.singletonMap("join", rootJoin));
    
    return query;
}

private Map<String, Object> buildJoinLevel(
        List<String> childIndexes,
        String parentField,
        String childField,
        Map<String, Object> nestedJoin) {
    
    Map<String, Object> joinQuery = new HashMap<>();
    joinQuery.put("indices", childIndexes);
    joinQuery.put("on", Arrays.asList(parentField, childField));
    
    Map<String, Object> childRequest = new HashMap<>();
    
    if (nestedJoin != null) {
        // Add nested join to child request
        childRequest.put("query", Collections.singletonMap("join", nestedJoin));
    } else {
        // Leaf level - just match all
        childRequest.put("query", Collections.singletonMap("match_all", new HashMap<>()));
    }
    
    joinQuery.put("request", childRequest);
    
    return joinQuery;
}
```

